## 3. Node Operations

### Start Node

```bash
cockroach start \
  --certs-dir=certs \
  --store=<path> \
  --listen-addr=<ip>:26257 \
  --http-addr=<ip>:8080 \
  --join=<node1>:26257,<node2>:26257,<node3>:26257 \
  --locality=region=<region>,zone=<zone>
```

### Stop (Drain) Node Gracefully

```bash
# Step 1: Drain — moves leases off, finishes in-flight queries
cockroach node drain <node-id> --certs-dir=certs --host=<ip>:26257
# Step 2: Wait for drain to complete (monitor output)
# Step 3: Stop the process
cockroach quit --certs-dir=certs --host=<ip>:26257
```

**❌ NEVER: `kill -9` a CockroachDB node unless absolutely necessary. Always drain first.**

### Add Node(s)

Start new node with `--join` pointing to existing nodes. The cluster auto-rebalances ranges to the new node. Monitor rebalancing progress in DB Console.

### Decommission Node(s)

```bash
# Move ALL replicas off the node, then mark it as decommissioned
cockroach node decommission <node-id> --certs-dir=certs --host=<ip>:26257
# Wait for completion — DO NOT stop the node until all replicas have moved
```

Monitor decommission progress:
```sql
SELECT node_id, is_decommissioning, draining, membership
FROM crdb_internal.gossip_liveness;
```

