## 4. Monitoring & Alert Thresholds

### Critical Alerts (Page Immediately)

| Alert | Condition | Action |
|-------|-----------|--------|
| Node down | `liveness.livenodes` decreased | Check node health, restart if needed |
| Ranges unavailable | `ranges.unavailable > 0` | Check node liveness, network partitions |
| Storage > 85% | `capacity.used / capacity > 0.85` | Add nodes or increase storage immediately |

### Warning Alerts (Investigate Within Hours)

| Alert | Condition | Action |
|-------|-----------|--------|
| Storage > 70% | `capacity.used / capacity > 0.7` | Plan capacity expansion |
| CPU > 80% sustained | `sys.cpu.combined.percent-normalized > 0.8` | Check for hot ranges, optimize queries |
| Under-replicated ranges | `ranges.underreplicated > 0` for > 30 min | Check node health, network, storage |
| LSM read amplification > 20 | `rocksdb.read-amplification > 20` | Check compaction queue, consider maintenance |
| Version mismatch | Nodes running different versions | Complete rolling upgrade |
| Certificate expiration | < 30 days to expiry | Rotate certificates |
| Changefeed lag | Lag exceeds SLA threshold | Check sink, increase memory budget |
| Intent buildup | `intentbytes` sustained growth > 100MB | Check for long-running transactions |
| High p99 latency | `sql.exec.latency-p99` > 3x baseline | Check contention, query plans |
| Transaction abort rate | `sql.txn.abort.count` spike | Check for contention patterns |

### Key Metrics to Export

```yaml
# Prometheus / Datadog / Grafana categories
Node Health:
  - sys.cpu.combined.percent-normalized
  - sys.rss  # resident memory
  - capacity.used / capacity
  - liveness.livenodes

SQL Performance:
  - sql.exec.latency-p99
  - sql.distsql.flows.active
  - sql.conn.latency-p99
  - sql.txn.abort.count

Replication:
  - ranges.unavailable  # CRITICAL if > 0
  - ranges.underreplicated
  - rebalancing.queriespersecond

Storage (LSM):
  - rocksdb.read-amplification
  - rocksdb.compactions
  - rocksdb.num-sstables

Intents:
  - intentcount
  - intentbytes
```

