## Anti-Pattern Quick Reference (Operator-Specific)

| ❌ Anti-Pattern | Why | ✅ Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `kill -9` without draining | In-flight queries interrupted, leases stuck | Always `cockroach node drain` first |
| Upgrade all nodes simultaneously | Risk of cluster unavailability | Rolling upgrade, one node at a time |
| Finalize version before all nodes upgraded | Cannot roll back | Upgrade ALL nodes, then `SET CLUSTER SETTING version` |
| No backup schedule | Data loss on failure | `CREATE SCHEDULE FOR BACKUP` |
| `root` user in production | No audit trail, unlimited permissions | Custom DBA role with scoped grants |
| No alerting on `ranges.unavailable` | Data unavailability goes undetected | Alert immediately if > 0 |
| Ignoring LSM read amplification | Queries degrade silently | Alert at > 20, investigate compaction |
| Overlapping key ranges in parallel DML | Serialization failures | Partition into disjoint ranges |
| Decommission without waiting | Replicas lost, under-replication | Wait for all replicas to move off |
| No clock sync (NTP) | Clock skew → transaction errors | Configure NTP, set `--max-offset` |
